  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying 'probable' outcomes (probability > 1/n) and averaging them. In this case, neither lottery has outcomes exceeding the threshold (100% for A, >50% for B), so the reason would not support either lottery. The individual, however, explicitly bases their choice on the 50% chance of zero loss in B, which suggests they are attending to the possibility of a favorable outcome, but not using a threshold rule to filter outcomes or computing averages of a subset. The mention of '50% chance no loss' aligns with noticing a specific outcome, but not with the full logic of the reason, which excludes outcomes at exactly 50%. Moreover, the individual’s justification includes non-normative factors like consistency and salience of unrelated information (2000 euros), which are unrelated to the reason. There is no evidence of applying a threshold rule or averaging probable outcomes. The information considered (presence of no-loss outcome, emotional salience, consistency) does not match the structured filtering and averaging required by the reason. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
